# arc .mailmap — Canonical identity mapping
#
# Maps historical committer name/email combinations to canonical arc identities.
# Consumed by `git shortlog`, `git log --use-mailmap`, and arc's own `arc auth`
# identity system when importing Git histories via `arc git-import`.
#
# Format:
#   Canonical Name <canonical@email>  Old Name <old@email>
#   Canonical Name <canonical@email>  <old@email>
#
# Examples:
#   Ada Lovelace <ada@example.com>  <ada.lovelace@oldemployer.com>
#   Ada Lovelace <ada@example.com>  A. Lovelace <a.lovelace@example.com>
#
# Arc identity note:
# arc's Ed25519 keypair is tied to the email supplied at `arc auth login`.
# If your email changes, add a mapping here so that `arc log` correctly
# attributes historical changes to your new canonical identity.
#
# Add contributor mappings below this line:
